From: SBE1V1K build <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] qualcommbe: sbe1v1k: drop the dp2..dp4 Ethernet aliases

The vendor APPSBL (U-Boot fdt_fixup_ethernet()) walks /aliases and, for
every "ethernet<N>" entry, injects env eth<N>addr into the referenced node
as local-mac-address.  The aliases in this board file therefore do not just
document probe order: they hand the bootloader control of the port MACs,
and the provisioning on some units sets eth1addr == eth2addr == eth3addr.
On such a unit eth1..eth3 come up with one identical global MAC and
addr_assign_type=0, which also silently disables sbe-lan-mac -- it only
rewrites kernel-random (locally administered) addresses.

Keep only the ethernet0 alias so eth0 still receives the per-unit base MAC
(env ethaddr).  dp2..dp4 then carry no MAC in the DT, nss-dp falls back to
eth_hw_addr_random() (addr_assign_type=1) and sbe-lan-mac pins
eth1..eth3 = eth0+1/+2/+3 before netifd builds br-lan.  Same layout and
same premise as the 24.10 overlay (ethernet-macs).

diff --git a/target/linux/qualcommbe/files/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq9574-sbe1v1k.dts b/target/linux/qualcommbe/files/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq9574-sbe1v1k.dts
--- a/target/linux/qualcommbe/files/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq9574-sbe1v1k.dts
+++ b/target/linux/qualcommbe/files/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq9574-sbe1v1k.dts
@@ -39,12 +39,17 @@
 
 	aliases {
 		serial0 = &blsp1_uart2;
-		/* S2 probe order: port 6 (RTL8261N 10G) first, then the
-		 * QCA8081 and two qca8075 ports.  eth0 = 10G LAN, eth1 = WAN. */
+		/* Only dp1.  The APPSBL (vendor U-Boot fdt_fixup_ethernet())
+		 * injects env eth<N>addr as local-mac-address into every node
+		 * aliased as ethernet<N>; units whose env carries identical
+		 * eth1addr..eth3addr then come up with eth1..eth3 sharing one
+		 * global MAC and addr_assign_type=0, which also defeats
+		 * sbe-lan-mac (it only rewrites kernel-random addresses).
+		 * Without the aliases dp2..dp4 get no MAC, nss-dp falls back
+		 * to eth_hw_addr_random() (addr_assign_type=1) and
+		 * sbe-lan-mac pins eth1..eth3 = eth0+1/+2/+3.  eth0 keeps the
+		 * bootloader-injected base MAC.  Do not re-add ethernet1..3. */
 		ethernet0 = "/soc@0/dp1";
-		ethernet1 = "/soc@0/dp2";
-		ethernet2 = "/soc@0/dp3";
-		ethernet3 = "/soc@0/dp4";
 	};
 
 	/*
